"""Original analysis for the issue5 price overlay; no copied primer prose."""
def render_reports(summary,lineage,audit,schedule,decks,teams,proposals,manifest):
    from recalibration_v3 import FAMILIES,table,CR_URL
    files={}
    team_by={(r['team'],r['model']):r for r in teams}
    compare=[]
    for t in 'ABCDEFGHI':
        a=team_by[t,'organizer_v2'];b=team_by[t,'candidate_v3']
        compare.append(dict(team=t,original=a['original_team'],organizer_v2=a['total'],candidate_v3=b['total'],delta_v3_from_v2=b['total']-a['total'],v3_heads=f"{b['head_a']}/{b['head_b']}",v3_over_120=b['team_overage'],v3_rank=b['rank_by_construction_cost']))
    price=lambda n,z='main':next(r for r in schedule if r['card_name']==n and r['zone']==z)
    high_names=['Intuition','Gifts Ungiven','Natural Order','Protean Hulk','Grim Tutor','Final Parting','Fabricate','Displacer Kitten','Necrotic Ooze','Chainer, Dementia Master','Candelabra of Tawnos','Panoptic Mirror','Time Warp','Malakir Rebirth // Malakir Mire','Urza, Lord High Artificer']
    high=[]
    for n in high_names:
        r=price(n,'commanders' if n=='Urza, Lord High Artificer' else 'main')
        high.append({k:r[k] for k in ('card_name','zone','old_effective_points','proposed_points','reason')})
    exact=[r for r in lineage if r['precision'] in ('organizer_explicit_numeric','explicit_organizer_price')]
    files['decision_taxonomy.md']='# Organizer decision taxonomy and precedence\n\n'
    files['decision_taxonomy.md']+=f"This pass reads all eleven B1–B3 reviews plus the premium-boundary ledger and consolidated166-row overlay. It preserves {len(lineage)} effective protected card/location decisions, including explicit nonchanges and earlier unsuperseded decisions. {len(exact)} rows are classified as explicit numeric from original provenance; other rows retain working/approximate status. These counts are decisions, not measured card-strength observations.\n\n"
    files['decision_taxonomy.md']+='The fifty historical0–5 anchors remain unchanged and are not numerical price bins. Later numeric decisions control only the named location. The full event chain and literal source mentions are in decision_lineage.csv; mentions may include superseded numbers and are not themselves the precedence algorithm. Broad family rows in the preview are assistant illustrations, not hundreds of organizer-approved exact prices.\n\n'
    files['decision_taxonomy.md']+='Authority order: historical schedule and earlier numeric exceptions → Batch1 A/B/C and land lock → accepted B1/B2 working overlay → Batch3 G → G follow-up → H → I → handoff explicit nonchanges. The166-row consolidation selects the latest working values. Additional research never overwrites these protected values. Source precision is corrected separately from price: Boseiju/Otawara6 are still selections within5–6 despite a raw numeric label; Reshape/Whir8 are approximate; Coffers9 is an accepted assistant placeholder, not a human-specified9; Heliod6/Sheoldred13 are working CZ choices.\n\n'
    files['decision_taxonomy.md']+='decision_reversals.csv distinguishes older prices from within-note considerations. Key reversals: Chant12→3→1, Basalt2→4, Swan3→2, Opposition8→6, KCI earlier12→10, Unwinding Clock3→2, Land Tax3→2→1, Crop Rotation initial7→6, Provisioner considered0→confirmed1. Bloodthirsty/Tenacity pending0 were replaced by3/4. Aluren2→4 is deliberately paired with free Acererak. Birthing Pod5 is now a working choice in5–6, not an invented exact6.\n\n'
    for f,(anchors,counter,why) in FAMILIES.items():
        files['decision_taxonomy.md']+=f'## {f}\n\n{why}\n\nComparisons: {anchors}.\n\nBoundary: {counter}\n\n'
    files['decision_taxonomy.md']+='No new coefficients were fitted. The four lenses guide explicit per-card judgments in proposals_v3.tsv: efficiency, resource conversion, opportunity cost and verified2HG delta. No point is added because a card appears frequently or merely participates in a combo. Price differences inside families are deliberate comparisons, not false precision from a regression.\n'

    files['global_recalibration_analysis.md']='# Global v3 recalibration results — season0-proposed\n\n'
    files['global_recalibration_analysis.md']+=f"Coverage: {summary['old_schedule_identities']} old schedule identities; {summary['benchmark_unique_identities']} unique cards in18 decks; mandatory union {summary['mandatory_union']}. The recorded audit contains {summary['recorded_audit_union']} identities, including {summary['additional_individual_proposal_identities']} additional individually proposed identities and {summary['additional_inherited_positive_identities']} inherited positive identities missing from the mandatory union. Oracle text screens nominated {summary['oracle_screen_nominees']} identities from {summary['commander_legal_oracle_population']} known Commander-legal Oracle identities. Screen nominations are not claims that a human independently rated each hit. The explicit proposal file has {summary['explicit_agent_proposals']} card/location judgments; {summary['changed_agent_prices']} differ from organizer-only v2.\n\n"
    files['global_recalibration_analysis.md']+=f"Candidate legal point-bearing identities: **{summary['legal_pointed_identities']}**, with {summary['legal_pointed_main']} main-deck locations and {summary['legal_pointed_commanders']} commander locations (overlap possible). All other verified identities retain their fixed historical/zero value; unknowns error. The schedule contains zero rows for important deliberate exceptions. Every legal positive backend price is represented, including twelve off-roster shock/surveil lands absent from the old export. Representative-printing digital/games flags are not Oracle-identity legality; Intuition and Pox demonstrate why that matters. This repairs coverage only and changes no historical file. No inherited impact score or cutoff was manipulated: >77.5 remains the old screening policy, while explicitly documented price overrides implement this review.\n\n"
    files['global_recalibration_analysis.md']+=f"Organizer-only v2 has {summary['organizer_v2_legal_pointed_identities']} legal pointed identities. Research adds {summary['newly_pointed_locations']} positive locations from zero and makes {summary['newly_unpointed_locations']} locations free. The larger difference from the old320-row export includes global organizer prices, inherited land-family picks and corrected coverage, not just new research. No natural power discontinuity is claimed at the retained cutoff.\n\n"
    files['global_recalibration_analysis.md']+=table(compare,['team','original','organizer_v2','candidate_v3','delta_v3_from_v2','v3_heads','v3_over_120','v3_rank'])
    files['global_recalibration_analysis.md']+='\nThese are construction-resource totals, not a ranking of competitive win chances. Old submitted lists were designed under different snapshots; comparing their raw old scores as though prices were common would be invalid. v2 applies all organizer decisions globally; v3 adds only research proposals. Every card copy uses the same Oracle/location value. No historical list was rebuilt.\n\n'
    files['global_recalibration_analysis.md']+='Team E remains the organizer\'s positive qualitative example. Its new total is not forced to120. A/B retain expensive fetch/original-dual mana bases; the original TeamA decks each use ten fetches and six original duals, already80 points per head at the retained5-point working values. H/G/I differences reflect globally shared edits, not their last intermediate review numbers.\n\n'
    for team in 'ABCDEFGHI':
        b=team_by[team,'candidate_v3'];dr=[r for r in decks if r['deck_id'].startswith(team)]
        files['global_recalibration_analysis.md']+=f"### Team {team}\n\n{dr[0]['deck_id']} top costs: {dr[0]['v3_top_drivers']}. {dr[1]['deck_id']} top costs: {dr[1]['v3_top_drivers']}. Total {b['total']}; over team cap by{b['team_overage']}; head overages{b['head_a_overage']}/{b['head_b_overage']}. Required transfer{b['transfer_required']}, legally transferrable at most{b['transferrable_points']}; these are not approved transfers when the team already fails caps.\n\n"
    files['global_recalibration_analysis.md']+='### Limits and sensitivity\n\nThe benchmark is eighteen selected, intentionally synergistic lists, not a random sample and not labelled game outcomes. The prices are human-calibrated policy judgments. A one-point change to a shared staple moves a team by up to2 because singleton is enforced independently per deck; a commander-only change moves only heads using that commander. Sparse cutoff families and explicitly free commanders create structural opportunities that a budget cannot fully predict. No inferential confidence interval is supplied for subjective prices; the included ±1/±2 scenario tables measure construction sensitivity only. Do not interpret their ranges as probabilistic confidence intervals.\n'

    files['card_family_reviews_v3.md']='# Family review and explicit counterexamples\n\n'
    files['card_family_reviews_v3.md']+='Every mandatory identity/location has an audit row, exact pinned Oracle text, retained or proposed value, and a comparison. Rows labelled Oracle_family_screen_and_prior_rationale_retained are systematic screens plus existing judgments, not a new expert verdict. Each explicit change has an individual reason.\n\n'
    for f,(anchor,counter,why) in FAMILIES.items():
        rr=[r for r in schedule if r['family']==f];pp=[r for r in rr if r['authority']=='agent_proposal_awaiting_approval']
        files['card_family_reviews_v3.md']+=f"## {f}\n\n{why} Reviewed {len(rr)} location rows; {len(pp)} new proposal rows. Anchor: {anchor}. Counterexample: {counter}\n\n"
        if pp:files['card_family_reviews_v3.md']+=table(pp,['card_name','zone','old_effective_points','proposed_points','anchor_comparison','reason'])+'\n'
    files['card_family_reviews_v3.md']+='The Natural Order/Rector/Hulk comparison prices cheating/assembly differently from narrow Trinket-family searches. Chainer/Ooze/Kitten carry reusable-engine costs, while Acererak and Devourer can be free payloads. Broad standalone usefulness is evidence of applicability, not automatic points. Cheap normal dorks, fair counterspells, weak MDFCs, and deliberately free land engines remain counterexamples.\n'

    files['exception_and_conflict_queue.md']='''# Organizer approval queue — no unilateral exceptions applied

1. **Time Sieve stays8.** The organizer reaffirmed8 and later considered more without choosing a number. Research alternative10 is NOT applied to v3. It creates an extra team turn but must sacrifice five artifacts controlled by the same head. A union of ally artifacts does not pay that cost. Compare new12-point one-card Time Warp. Whether8 remains sufficient is a Season0 testing decision.
2. **Winds of Abandon stays working5.** Overload exiles every creature the caster does not control, including ally creatures. Research alternative2–3 may be defensible because the original opponent-only premise was false; not applied. Non-overload targets a creature the caster does not control, so it may target an ally too. The basic-land searches can interact with Opposition Agent, but do not erase friendly exile.
3. **Free and very cheap commanders.** Najeela, Kenrith, Inalla, Yuriko and Oloro remain free where explicitly preserved; Chulane stays2 and Derevi stays working2 despite earlier qualitative0. Proposed Gitrog6, Shorikai4, Breya5, Talion4, Lavinia4 and Urza8 are separate agent judgments awaiting review. No blanket2x rule. Sheoldred13 and Heliod6 remain assistant-selected working numbers, not exact approvals.
4. **Tutor hierarchy tension.** Instant-to-hand Eladamri's Call4 is cheaper than top-of-library Worldly6; universal Enlightened9 exceeds some broader tutors with slower/conditional costs. Preserve the human assignments; do not claim a perfectly monotonic objective strength scale. New analogues must show constraints, not force every tutor to4 or higher.
5. **Land burden.** Fetches/original duals5 working strongly tax original A/B mana bases. No automatic decrease or new nonbasic tax is introduced. Basic, slow and conditional fixing remaining free may be intentional opportunity-cost incentives; original conceptual team E is not forced into budget by adjusting lands.
6. **Symmetric attrition and locks.** Pox, Smallpox, Death Cloud and Contamination remain0. Fraying Omnipotence proposed0 extends that rationale but is NOT an explicit organizer price. Strong offensive combinations may still be legal; no blanket infinite-combo or turn-seven prohibition is introduced.
7. **Approximate inputs.** Coffers9 originated as assistant8–10 placeholder; Bloodletter~5 and Wound~2 are approximate. Replenish9 is a9-or10 pick; Academy Rector9 is midpoint8–10; Scepter4 was assistant-selected after an unspecified increase. Keep all as working choices while awaiting exact decisions.
8. **Tail/discovery review.** Some inherited positive cards and free Oracle-screen nominations lack new individual expert evidence. The audit says so. Screen membership and deterministic pricing are not validation. Review high-risk remaining names before freezing the schedule; do not convert every query hit into points.
9. **Consecrated Sphinx remains the organizer's explicit1 from October20.** A research idea of7 reflects the four offered cards from two ordinary enemy draws and comparison with Rhystic9, but was rejected by the protected-price guard and is NOT applied. Its six-mana deployment and creature vulnerability are material counterarguments. Ask the organizer rather than silently overruling the original decision.
10. **Timetwister remains working3 inside the older organizer-approved2–3 range.** A proposed5 to match newer Wheel5 was not applied. The newest Wheel increase does not silently expand Timetwister's own earlier range. This creates an intentional family inconsistency requiring organizer review.

11. **Cheap risky extra turns stay7.** Last Chance and Warrior's Oath are explicit7; Final Fortune retains working7 within organizer at-least6 guidance. They may compare favorably with proposed12-point five-mana turns, but delayed team loss is real. A research alternative9–12 requires review and is not applied. Expropriate also stays explicit8 despite two possible friendly time votes.

All proposals are season0-proposed, activated=false. The PR neither enacts these alternatives nor changes decklists, ban policy, rules, budgets or prices outside the new research snapshot.
'''

    files['organizer_audio_summary.md']='# Read-aloud organizer summary\n\n'
    files['organizer_audio_summary.md']+='We have now priced all eighteen original decks under one common organizer snapshot, then under a separate researched proposal. The decks are unchanged. The largest misses were efficient tutors, broad repeatable engines, and guaranteed commander access. We kept deliberate exceptions: Pox and Contamination are free, Acererak is free, and Aluren costs four. We did not double all commander prices or charge every combo component.\n\n'
    for i,row in enumerate(high,1):
        location='in the command zone' if row['zone']=='commanders' else 'in the main deck'
        files['organizer_audio_summary.md']+=f"{i}. {row['card_name']}, {location}, goes from {row['old_effective_points']} to {row['proposed_points']} proposed points. {row['reason']}\n\n"
    files['organizer_audio_summary.md']+='The same extra turn gives both teammates a turn. That is why the three equivalent five-mana turn spells are proposed at twelve. Savor the Moment is lower because both friendly players skip untapping. Chainer, Ooze and Kitten are priced as reusable engines. The payload can still be free.\n\n'
    files['organizer_audio_summary.md']+='All nine teams originally cost120. Under organizer-only prices, followed by the research candidate, totals are:\n\n'
    for row in compare:files['organizer_audio_summary.md']+=f"Team {row['team']}: {row['organizer_v2']} becomes {row['candidate_v3']}.\n\n"
    files['organizer_audio_summary.md']+='These totals do not measure win probabilities. Team E remains the positive qualitative benchmark even when its repriced cost exceeds120. Decisions still needed include Time Sieve above8, Winds of Abandon after correcting friendly fire, free commander exceptions, and precise working ranges. Next, approve or revise the proposed card prices, then authorize a separate rebuild of E alongside one engine-heavy team under the unchanged120/72/12 constraints. Play paired games before claiming the schedule achieves a target bracket. No current deck was rebuilt to make these numbers look balanced.\n'

    files['README_v3.md']='''# Global recalibration v3 — Issue #5

Status: season0-proposed, activated=false. Feature branch targets commander-doubles-deck-benchmarks. Read organizer_audio_summary.md, global_recalibration_analysis.md, decision_taxonomy.md and exception_and_conflict_queue.md first.

The effective organizer v2 overlay is authoritative for this experiment, with explicit nonchanges and prior unsuperseded decisions preserved. Candidate v3 adds individually documented proposals_v3.tsv rows. That file is editable research input, not organizer approval. Original320-row schedule, all50 qualitative observations, all18 decklists and historical scores stay immutable.

## Reproduce from repository root

```sh
python -m pip install -r commander-doubles-deck-benchmarks/requirements.txt
python commander-doubles-deck-benchmarks/recalibration/recalibration_v3.py
python commander-doubles-deck-benchmarks/recalibration/recalibration_v3.py --check
python commander-doubles-deck-benchmarks/recalibration/validate_recalibration_v3.py
python commander-doubles-deck-benchmarks/recalibration/score_recalibration_v3.py commander-doubles-deck-benchmarks/batch3/decks/H1.txt --deck-b commander-doubles-deck-benchmarks/batch3/decks/H2.json --model candidate-v3 --summary
```

The validation command runs all56 preserved Batch suites, the new global suite, and byte reproduction, then records actual results in validation_results_v3.json. The example H team exits1 because it exceeds budget. Use the existing Python dependencies. The offline scorer score_recalibration_v3.py accepts a deck path, optional --deck-b, --model organizer-v2 or candidate-v3, --summary and --export. Exit0 means legal and within cap; exit1 means construction/budget noncompliance, and exit2 means invalid input. It never certifies gameplay legality. Ordinary regeneration/scoring is offline. Source commit and file checksums are in source_provenance.json. All complete JSON deck inventories are read from original Batch1/2/3 folders and never rewritten. Full_card_rescoring_ledger has1800 rows, with quantities expanded to one row per physical card and three comparable prices per row. The primary schedule has one row per Oracle identity and construction zone. Ineligible command zones are not priced. Unknown identities and negative/noninteger prices fail; Known free cards stay free. Edit proposals_v3.tsv, then regenerate; exported CSVs are derived outputs, not editable active inputs. Naming uses the existing Oracle resolver plus a local face-alias extension; back-face names still resolve to one Oracle identity.

Columns separate raw organizer labels from provenance-corrected exact/working status. decision_lineage preserves prior events and literal source mentions; it does not turn every incidental preview-row zero into a human approval. family_coverage_audit identifies individually proposed, organizer-reviewed and inherited/screened rows. targeted_oracle_discovery includes nominations that are not fully rated; unpriced_high_risk_queue explicitly marks that limitation.

No coefficients were learned from the eighteen decks, no per-deck normalization was used, and no sample outcome data was fabricated. Prices are auditable comparative judgments. No known combo or teammate pairing increases a construction price automatically. The old impact cutoff is preserved, while named price exceptions form the new versioned overlay. A card's legal status is independent of points and all existing bans remain.

The official rule landing/ban list and two primary combo examples were read2026-10-22. Oracle text is the pinned October20 dataset; a failed Scryfall web retrieval is recorded and no new full bulk update is claimed. Current CR805.8 and810.9 support the team-turn/life analyses, while original Batches1–3 controller cases remain accessible. See v3_inputs/research_evidence.json and rules_verification_v3.md for source-specific conclusions and unresolved strength judgments.
'''
    return files
